To evaluate the integral \( \int_{-\infty}^\infty \frac{x \cdot \cos(x)}{x^2+4} \, dx \), we first note that the integrand is an odd function. An odd function \( f(x) \) satisfies \( f(-x) = -f(x) \). Checking this property:

