To determine the radius of convergence for the series \(\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{x^{n}}{n^{2}{(5+\cos(n\pi/3))^{n}}}\), we use the root test. The general term \(a_n\) is \(\frac{1}{n^{2}{(5+\cos(n\pi/3))^{n}}}\).

The radius of convergence \(R\) is given by:
\[
R = \frac{1}{\limsup_{n \to \infty} |a_n|^{1/n}}
\]

First, compute \(|a_n|^{1/n}\):
\[
|a_n|^{1/n} = \left( \frac{1}{n^{2}{(5+\cos(n\pi/3))^{n}}} \right)^{1/n} = \frac{1}{n^{2/n} (5 + \cos(n\pi/3))}
\]

