To evaluate the limit \( \lim_{x \rightarrow 0^+} \exp\left(-\frac{1}{x}\right)\ln\left(\frac{1}{x^2}\right) \), we start by rewriting the logarithmic term using logarithm properties:

\[
\ln\left(\frac{1}{x^2}\right) = -2 \ln x
\]

