Let $G$ be a profinite group. Consider the Grothendieck group $K(G,\mathbb{Z}_\ell)$ of the derived category of finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}_\ell$-modules with continuous $G$-action, and the Grothendieck group $K(G,\mathbb{F}_\ell)$ of the derived category of finitely generated $\mathbb{F}_\ell$-modules with continuous $G$-action. The map $[T] \mapsto [T \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\ell}^L \mathbb{F}_\ell]$ defines a group homomorphism $K(G,\mathbb{Z}_\ell) \to K(G,\mathbb{F}_\ell)$, known as the reduction map. If $T$ is a $\mathbb{Z}_\ell$-module with continuous $G$-action such that $T$ is killed by some power of $\ell$, is it true that $[T \otimes^L_{\mathbb{Z}_\ell} \mathbb{F}_\ell] = 0$ in $K(G,\mathbb{F}_\ell)$? Write your answer in \boxed{} format.<|im_end|>
